---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Accurate Online Compass privacy policy. All sensor and location data is processed locally in your browser — we collect no personal data and use no trackers."
	path="/privacy/"
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-24">
		<p class="eyebrow">legal</p>
		<h1 class="mt-4 text-display-lg text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mute">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}</p>

		<div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-body">
			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">In short</h2>
				<p class="leading-7">
					Accurate Online Compass is designed to be private by default. All sensor data — device
					orientation, magnetometer, and location — is processed locally in your browser and is
					never transmitted, stored, or shared. We do not use cookies, trackers, or analytics.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">What we collect</h2>
				<p class="leading-7 mb-3">We collect nothing. Specifically:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7">
					<li>No account, sign-up, or email is required.</li>
					<li>No personal information is requested or stored.</li>
					<li>Device orientation, heading, and GPS coordinates never leave your device.</li>
					<li>No third-party analytics or advertising SDKs are used.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">Browser permissions</h2>
				<p class="leading-7">
					The tools request sensor and location permissions through your browser to provide
					readings. You control these permissions at any time in your browser or operating
					system settings. Denying location permission still allows you to use every tool with
					manually entered coordinates.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">Local storage</h2>
				<p class="leading-7">
					Your theme preference (dark or light mode) is stored in your browser's local storage
					so your choice persists between visits. No other data is stored.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">Hosting</h2>
				<p class="leading-7">
					The website itself is served from standard web hosting infrastructure. Like any website,
					the hosting provider may keep routine server logs (such as IP addresses and requested
					URLs) for security and operational purposes. These logs are not used to identify you.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3">Contact</h2>
				<p class="leading-7">
					Questions about this policy? Reach us via the <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline decoration-link/30 hover:decoration-link">contact page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>